{"ts": 1791254635.576214, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the Friday build requirements: you need to define your environment (state, observations, actions, dynamics) and report pass^k on at least 3 seeds. The readings for week 3 cover environments and evaluation, and the key evaluation idea is that pass^k means all k runs succeed, which is about reliability.\n\nSince you said you're stuck on the eval part, I can help you work through the difference between pass@k and pass^k, then quiz you on it. First question: why do you think pass^k is the more relevant metric if the build is about dependable behavior?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=6 messages 2m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9113219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
